<xml xmlns="https://developers.google.com/blockly/xml"><variables><variable id="rainbow-pixel">led</variable><variable id="rainbow-hue">hue</variable></variables><block type="program_start" id="rainbow-start" x="50" y="50"><comment pinned="false" h="105" w="380">Connect the data input of the strip with 8 NeoPixel LEDs to GPIO 29. Power the strip according to its type and connect the strip GND to the board GND.</comment><next><block type="neopixel_init" id="rainbow-init-strip"><comment pinned="false" h="70" w="330">Initialize a strip with eight addressable NeoPixel LEDs on GPIO 29.</comment><value name="pin"><shadow type="math_number" id="rainbow-pin"><field name="NUM">29</field></shadow></value><value name="number"><shadow type="math_number" id="rainbow-count"><field name="NUM">8</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="rainbow-reset-hue"><field name="VAR" id="rainbow-hue">hue</field><comment pinned="false" h="107" w="758">Initial hue value. Think of hue as a color wheel containing all the colors of the rainbow.

https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/hue</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="rainbow-hue-zero"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><next><block type="text_print" id="rainbow-ready-print"><value name="TEXT"><shadow type="text" id="rainbow-ready-text"><field name="TEXT">NeoPixel rainbow</field></shadow></value></block></next></block></next></block></next></block><block type="program_loop" id="rainbow-loop" x="51" y="278"><comment pinned="false" h="85" w="350">Assign each LED a hue shifted by 45°. This spreads the eight LEDs evenly around the entire color wheel.</comment><statement name="DO"><block type="controls_for" id="rainbow-for-pixels"><field name="VAR" id="rainbow-pixel">led</field><comment pinned="false" h="54" w="317">A loop that makes 8 passes (0-7)
On each pass, the LED variable increases by 1</comment><value name="FROM"><shadow type="math_number" id="rainbow-from"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><value name="TO"><shadow type="math_number" id="rainbow-to"><field name="NUM">7</field></shadow></value><value name="BY"><shadow type="math_number" id="rainbow-by"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value><statement name="DO"><block type="neopixel_control" id="rainbow-set-pixel"><comment pinned="false" h="100" w="360">Convert the HSL color to RGB. Modulo 360 keeps the calculated hue within the color-wheel range.</comment><value name="address"><block type="variables_get" id="rainbow-pixel-address"><field name="VAR" id="rainbow-pixel">led</field><comment pinned="false" h="72" w="216">Specifies the NeoPixel position.
0 is the first NeoPixel.
7 is the last NeoPixel.</comment></block></value><value name="color"><block type="HSL_to_RGB" id="rainbow-hsl-color"><comment pinned="false" h="81" w="302">Converts hue, saturation, and lightness to an RGB color. The allowed variable ranges are shown in square brackets.</comment><value name="hue"><block type="math_modulo" id="rainbow-pixel-hue-modulo"><value name="DIVIDEND"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="rainbow-pixel-hue-add"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="89" w="252">Add an offset to the base hue for each LED so that every LED has a different hue and together they form a rainbow.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="rainbow-base-hue"><field name="VAR" id="rainbow-hue">hue</field></block></value><value name="B"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="rainbow-pixel-offset"><field name="OP">MULTIPLY</field><comment pinned="false" h="48" w="292">Each NeoPixel hue is shifted by 45° around the color wheel.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="rainbow-pixel-index"><field name="VAR" id="rainbow-pixel">led</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="rainbow-hue-step"><field name="NUM">45</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></value><value name="DIVISOR"><shadow type="math_number" id="rainbow-circle"><field name="NUM">360</field></shadow></value></block></value><value name="saturation"><shadow type="math_number" id="rainbow-saturation"><field name="NUM">100</field></shadow></value><value name="lightness"><shadow type="math_number" id="rainbow-lightness"><field name="NUM">50</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></statement><next><block type="neopixel_write" id="rainbow-show"><comment pinned="false" h="65" w="320">After setting all eight LEDs, send all colors to the strip at once.</comment><next><block type="math_change" id="rainbow-increment-hue"><field name="VAR" id="rainbow-hue">hue</field><comment pinned="false" h="75" w="363">On each pass, shift the hue by 3 steps.

Changing the hue creates a smooth moving rainbow.</comment><value name="DELTA"><shadow type="math_number" id="rainbow-animation-step"><field name="NUM">3</field></shadow></value><next><block type="utime.delay" id="rainbow-delay"><field name="SCALE">sleep_ms</field><comment pinned="false" h="53" w="409">A short delay so the animation is not too fast.</comment><value name="TIME"><shadow type="math_number" id="rainbow-delay-time"><field name="NUM">20</field></shadow></value></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></statement></block>
  <!--ESPIDE_EXTENSIONS_BEGIN-->
eyJ2ZXJzaW9uIjoxLCJwcm9jZXNzb3IiOiJTaW11bGF0b3IiLCJleHRlbnNpb25zIjpbXX0=
